#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# hankel_transform

#% text
# `hankel_transform(f, r, s)` gives the Hankel transform of order 0, `integrate(f bessel_j(0, s r) r, [r, 0, inf])`; `hankel_transform(f, r, s, nu)` the transform of order nu.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Closed forms for sums of `c r^mu`, `c r^mu exp(-a r)`, `c r^mu exp(-a r^2)`, `c r^nu (r^2 + a^2)^-p` and `g(r) dirac_delta(r - b)` (DLMF 10.22; Erdelyi et al., Tables of Integral Transforms II). Other functions leave the transform unevaluated.

#% item
# A numeric s evaluates the closed form at s.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
hankel_transform(exp(-r^2), r, s)
#% output
#= (1/2)*exp((-1/4)*s^2)

#% cell
hankel_transform(1/sqrt(1 + r^2), r, s)
#% output
#= exp(-s)/s

#% cell
hankel_transform(1/r^3, r, s)
#% output
#= -s

#% cell
hankel_transform(r^2*dirac_delta(r - 2), r, s)
#% output
#= 8*bessel_j(0, 2*s)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `inverse_hankel_transform`, `bessel_j`, `fourier_transform`
